result: 'Added tests/scoped_identity.rs: 5 hermetic end-to-end conformance tests driving
  the real `jinnc build` binary against on-disk multi-package projects (private HOME
  + pre-populated git cache, no network). Covers the four scope.md behaviors observable
  at the build boundary: (1) single-version scoped dep build+run §2.1/2.2; (2) public
  transitive reach-in via `use baz/bar` §4; (3) internal reach-in hard error with
  the documented visibility-ceiling diagnostic §4.1; (4) two-live-majors hard reject
  with the documented multi-version diagnostic §5; plus same-major minor-diff acceptance.
  All 5 pass. No source changes required (the full scoped-identity pipeline was already
  landed through v126). Verified green: lib 318, bulk 912, access_semantics 11, concurrency
  20, std_stable 2, traits 7. Pre-existing unrelated failures (integration.rs column_max/min/sum
  @column aggregation) confirmed independent of this work and recorded as a separate
  pitfall.'
description: 'Add integration tests covering scoped identity end-to-end: path resolution,
  reexport consent (legal and reach-in error cases), and multi-version (deferred-or-implemented
  per Q4). Done when the full test suite passes and satisfies the definition of done.
  Depends on all threading, resolution, reexport, multi-version, and codegen subtasks.'
